<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-miranda-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila miranda detail-scale Turing wavelength (1.9 µm, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 89.4/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the 1.864 µm field and adds the dispersion comparison (Pearson r = 0.999999996, RMSE = 1.65e-5), a monotonic √D_u sweep, an equal-diffusion ablation, plate segmentation (foreground 0.370, coherency 0.806, circularity 0.054), and an orientation-histogram KS of 0.333 against the pure field. The GIF is 12 frames at 640×480. CV similarity of the last frame to the plate is 86.7. Overall 89.4/100 (faithfulness 88.9, reproducibility 90.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 91, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 91. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_miranda_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-miranda-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 576855 B, 1464×912 px, artifact_sha256 d7278ebb5fca3418b98c565fdd094af5c3aa3e21abb8efb0337b276adcdd1078 (sha256 d7278ebb5fca3418b98c565fdd094af5c3aa3e21abb8efb0337b276adcdd1078), spec_fingerprint d72df4485d107fdd15f1f53825f9d2fc9fb6708a151467f2a51b6d54ce339010. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: d72df4485d107fdd15f1f53825f9d2fc9fb6708a151467f2a51b6d54ce339010; artifact_sha256: d7278ebb5fca3418b98c565fdd094af5c3aa3e21abb8efb0337b276adcdd1078; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_miranda_turing_wavelength_s0/Drosophila_miranda_specimen.jpg=fc43a0abd39eea68..., datasets/drosophila_miranda_turing_wavelength_s0/README.md=144d0cc17c40ba2e..., datasets/drosophila_miranda_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_miranda_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=03f46b7405f11c6b..., datasets/drosophila_miranda_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=ba21cc5176da73b5..., datasets/drosophila_miranda_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=e67dc1eb5bd042c5...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-miranda-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) dispersion relation. | Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics. | Shoup (1966) subcellular pigment granules in D. melanogaster. | Bachtrog (2008, 2013) neo-Y degeneration in D. miranda, with no 1.9 µm measurement.; reconstructed_in_script: D_u = 0.028630 and D_v = 0.274882 µm²/time so λ_max = 1.864 µm. | At 0 Ma, λ increases melanogaster 1.412 µm → miranda 1.864 µm → mojavensis 2.286 µm. | Equal-diffusion run collapses (std ratio about 4.9e-5). | Overlay depth 0.36 selected because the CV sweep stayed above 86 at every tested depth.; transfer_boundary: Image fitness compares the GIF last frame to the species-gallery plate, not to an EM of granules.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a second independent assessor scored this audit. | Does not claim the gallery plate is a micrograph of D. miranda pigment granules. | Does not claim geological time separates these three extant species; age is 0 Ma for all three.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [independent_assessor/model-fidelity, pressure P=0.9]: Second assessor was not available in this cloud loop.",
        "open need [specimen_comparison/specimen-match, pressure P=2.2]: Replace the gallery plate with a CC micrograph of miranda pigment granules if one is published.",
        "remediation needed: A second assessor has not scored this script. The single-agent limit is recorded, not treated as a pass.",
        "remediation needed: No transmission electron micrograph of D. miranda pigment granules was found; the gallery plate remains the fitness target." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.94e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

